  "body": "What happens: a 2D Pocket rest pass with a corner relief (#2400) cuts the relief at only some corners. The other corners keep their material. No note or warning tells the user.\n\nExpected: the rest pass cuts a relief at each inside corner that the rest area touches. If it cannot cut one, it says so in a note.\n\nEvidence:\n- The pocket is 30 x 30 mm with sharp corners. The rest tool is 6 mm, with `CornerReliefKind::Dogbone`. The entered previous tool is 16 mm.\n- `pocket_relief_plan` gives 4 reliefs, with the start points (3,3), (27,3), (3,27) and (27,27).\n- `rest_pocket_with_relief` cuts only the relief at (3,3).\n- The cause is the filter in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/rest2d.rs` (`rest_pocket_with_relief` on main): `.filter(|r| plan.center.contains(r.start))`. Each start point is on the boundary of `plan.center`. `Region::contains` gives `true` for (3,3) and `false` for the other three.\n- The plain pocket (`pocket_entered_with_relief`) cuts all 4 reliefs. The rest pass where the previous tool fits nowhere also cuts all 4.\n\nFound while I merged main into PR #2822 (#2033). The test `crates/motion/tests/rest_relief.rs` on that branch shows the result. It pins that the two rest modes agree, and does not pin the count of 4.\n\nWorkaround: use a plain pocket with the relief, not a rest pass.\n\nDone means: a rest pass with a relief cuts each relief whose corner the rest area touches. A test pins all 4 dogbone ends on the fixture above. A relief that the pass cannot cut gives a note.\n",
